  "details": "How to trigger this issue:\n\n1. Press [ Win+Blankspace ] switch to English keyboard layout (US keyboard)\n\n2. start VRChat\n\n3. Press [ Win+Blankspace ] switch to Microsoft Pinyin (Chinese IME)\n\n4. Press Y to open Chatbox, and try to type in something,then you will see IME doesn't input anything. \n\nHow to workaround:\n\n1. Make sure that switch to None-English IME first, then start VRChat\n\n2. OSC input is also a solution.\n\nTips:  My friend said Japanese also have the same issue. Looks like it's a general issue for all none-english languages. But I don't use Japanese IME so I can't check it by myself. :(",
